## Choosing a Lumens Tier for Your Room

Lumens measure how bright the projected image needs to be to stay legible against the light already in the room, and this is the single biggest factor competitors leave out of their pricing pages entirely. We publish two real tiers:

-   **3000 lumens, on the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/)**: a high brightness projector paired with a 2x2m screen, built for a standard boardroom, private salon or hotel suite where the room lighting is normal or can be dimmed for the presentation.

-   **5000 lumens, laser, on the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/)**: a Full HD laser projector built to stay crisp in a room that stays lit, such as a dealership showroom during a launch or a press conference where photographers need working light.

We do not publish a specific projector brand or a DLP or LCD technology type for either tier. We publish Full HD resolution on the Product Presentation Pack's laser tier. We do not publish a resolution figure for the Basic MICE Pack's 3000 lumen tier. If your venue has an unusual amount of ambient light or natural daylight, [contact us](/contact/) with the details so we can confirm which tier actually fits it, rather than guess. For the rest of our specialized and niche equipment layer, from moving head lighting to special effects, see our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) guide.

## Why the Screen Is Always Bundled With the Projector

We do not sell a projection screen as a standalone item, and we do not sell a projector without one. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) treats "projector & projection screen" as a single 50 euro add on line, and both the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) and the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) list the screen and the projector as one bundled inclusion, not two separate ones. The largest screen we publish is the Basic MICE Pack's 2x2m screen. We do not offer a bigger a la carte size.

This is a deliberate scope decision, not an oversight: a mismatched screen and projector produces a worse result than either sold separately, so we do not offer that combination. It's also why we treat projector rental and projection screen rental as one package, never two separate line items.

## Connecting Your Own Devices

Most presentations run off the presenter's own laptop, tablet or media player, not ours. On the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), we provide all necessary adapters, HDMI and USB-C, plus audio interfaces to connect your equipment to our screen and sound system, so the walkthrough on arrival is confirming the connection, not solving it on the spot.

## What We Don't Offer

We do not offer outdoor projection mapping or facade projection onto a building, which some Malaga competitors specialize in. That falls outside our current catalog. We do not stock an LED video wall as a projector alternative: this is a projector and screen setup, not a modular tiled display. We also do not publish 4K resolution on either projector tier, and we do not name a specific projector brand, since the honest answer is a spec tier, not a model.

